          "id": "ab-p1",
          "name": "Ab p1",
          "styles": {
            "color": "var(--ink-soft)",
            "margin": "0 0 16px",
            "max-width": "68ch"
          },
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Nell learned to throw at evening classes, then spent three years as an apprentice in a country pottery before setting up her own wheel in 2016. The barn now holds two wheels, a glaze kitchen and a gas kiln she built with a friend."
        },
        "ab-p2": {
          "attrs": {},
          "breakpoints": {},
          "children": [],
          "id": "ab-p2",
          "name": "Ab p2",
          "styles": {
            "color": "var(--ink-soft)",
            "margin": "0 0 16px",
            "max-width": "68ch"
          },
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "The clay is a buff stoneware from a supplier two counties away, and the glazes are mixed here from simple recipes: wood ash, iron, cobalt and a little patience."
        },
